WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:03.052
Here's how to read the Trade Levels Pro daily plan.

00:03.042 --> 00:08.735
The bias, what has to happen, the long levels, the targets, and where the idea is wrong.

00:08.725 --> 00:11.402
It's simpler than it looks, and it reads in order.

00:11.602 --> 00:15.119
Start with the bias. Bullish, bearish, or neutral.

00:15.109 --> 00:19.128
It's the day's lean. Neutral means no edge until price shows you one.

00:19.328 --> 00:21.539
Next, what has to happen to go long.

00:21.529 --> 00:26.414
Usually it's a failed breakdown. Price flushes below a level and traps the sellers,

00:26.404 --> 00:27.417
then reclaims it.

00:27.617 --> 00:30.531
Then the best long levels, ranked best first.

00:30.521 --> 00:32.126
Long 1 is the main spot.

00:32.116 --> 00:36.117
Long 2 and Long 3 are deeper backups if the first one fails.

00:36.317 --> 00:39.611
Don't buy the flush. Nobody knows where the bottom is yet.

00:39.601 --> 00:42.593
Wait for price to reclaim the level and hold above it.

00:42.583 --> 00:45.494
That's your trigger. Now you have a clear spot to be wrong.

00:45.694 --> 00:47.245
Targets are the next levels up.

00:47.235 --> 00:51.243
Take them level to level. Scale out at the first one, and trail a runner.

00:51.843 --> 00:56.078
Every long idea also has an invalidation level. The line where it's wrong.

00:56.068 --> 00:58.352
If price loses it, the long is off.

00:58.342 --> 01:01.858
You stand aside. No reclaim, no trade, either.

01:02.058 --> 01:07.929
So, in order. Bias. What has to happen. The levels. The targets. And where it's wrong.

01:07.919 --> 01:10.653
Read it the night before, then react to price.

01:10.853 --> 01:12.090
Full plan available.

01:12.080 --> 01:16.046
